{"post_stream":{"posts":[{"id":493009,"name":"","username":"doughy","avatar_template":"https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/d/c77e96/{size}.png","created_at":"2026-09-16T15:07:36.382Z","cooked":"\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-493009-where-does-the-bug-appear-featureproduct-1\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-493009-where-does-the-bug-appear-featureproduct-1\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eWhere does the bug appear (feature/product)?\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eGrok Bot\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-493009-describe-the-bug-2\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-493009-describe-the-bug-2\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eDescribe the Bug\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eSummary\u003cbr\u003e\nupdate_state with target: memory fails on every bot I tested with the exact error:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003ebrain docs snapshot was cut short before completing\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eSettings updates via update_state still work. Direct file writes to memory/profile.md and memory/log/*.md still work. Failed memory writes do not reliably land the fact.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWhere it happens\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eRecreated / reimported bots (e.g. after sidebar Delete + reimport): CreateAgent often leaves incomplete agent-data — missing memory/ folder, no conversation-blobs.db, empty latestRootBlobId. Scaffolding memory/ alone does not fix update_state.\u003cbr\u003e\nLong-lived bots too same error. So this is not recreate-only and not explained by one oversized chat.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eRepro\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eOpen any bot (fresh or old).\u003cbr\u003e\nAsk it to run update_state → target: memory, action: write, short log/note fact.\u003cbr\u003e\nObserve tool error: brain docs snapshot was cut short before completing.\u003cbr\u003e\nConfirm the fact is absent from memory/*.md (unless the bot file-appended as a workaround).\u003cbr\u003e\nOptionally: update_state → target: settings still succeeds on the same bot.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eExpected\u003cbr\u003e\nMemory write succeeds; fact appears in agent memory / prompt snapshots.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eActual\u003cbr\u003e\nTool errors; brain-docs snapshot aborts; store prompt snapshots can lag disk; bots fall back to editing memory/*.md by hand.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eNotes from local investigation\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eSQLite stores integrity-check OK; disk not full; agent-data → sand-data symlink fine.\u003cbr\u003e\nHost shows related brain-docs diagnostics (brain_docs_compensation_failed / brain_docs_channel_config_corrupt).\u003cbr\u003e\nBox host stamp observed: 332d021b.\u003cbr\u003e\nExample agent ids: CoS f283b3c0-75c5-41ac-a60b-455ef252740e; also reproduced on Economist and a brand-new Engineer.\u003cbr\u003e\nAlready filed in-app feedback (privacy mode blocked SendFeedback from the bot; filed via Help → Send Feedback).\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWorkaround\u003cbr\u003e\nFile-append durable facts to memory/profile.md / memory/log/YYYY-MM.md until fixed. Do not recommend Update/Reset Computer as the first fix for this (looks harness/brain-docs side).\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-493009-steps-to-reproduce-3\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-493009-steps-to-reproduce-3\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eSteps to Reproduce\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eOpen any bot (fresh or old).\u003cbr\u003e\nAsk it to run update_state → target: memory, action: write, short log/note fact.\u003cbr\u003e\nObserve tool error: brain docs snapshot was cut short before completing.\u003cbr\u003e\nConfirm the fact is absent from memory/*.md (unless the bot file-appended as a workaround).\u003cbr\u003e\nOptionally: update_state → target: settings still succeeds on the same bot.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-493009-expected-behavior-4\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-493009-expected-behavior-4\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eExpected Behavior\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eMemory write succeeds; fact appears in agent memory / prompt snapshots.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-493009-operating-system-5\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-493009-operating-system-5\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eOperating System\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eMacOS\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-493009-version-information-6\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-493009-version-information-6\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eVersion Information\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eVersion: 0.53.0\u003cbr\u003e\nRelease Track: stable\u003cbr\u003e\nOS: darwin\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-493009-does-this-stop-you-from-using-cursor-7\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-493009-does-this-stop-you-from-using-cursor-7\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eDoes this stop you from using Cursor\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eNo - Cursor works, but with this issue\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":1,"post_type":1,"posts_count":4,"updated_at":"2026-09-16T15:23:24.596Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":13,"reads":5,"readers_count":4,"score":66.0,"yours":false,"topic_id":171895,"topic_slug":"grok-bot-update-state-memory-writes-fail-fleet-wide-brain-docs-snapshot-was-cut-short-before-completing","display_username":"","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":2,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"read":true,"user_title":null,"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":138199,"hidden":false,"trust_level":0,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":false,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/grok-bot-update-state-memory-writes-fail-fleet-wide-brain-docs-snapshot-was-cut-short-before-completing/171895/1","reactions":[],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":0,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null,"can_vote":false},{"id":493081,"name":"Dean Rie","username":"deanrie","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/forum.cursor.com/deanrie/{size}/1263_2.png","created_at":"2026-09-16T16:04:25.114Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eHey, thanks for the detailed report. It really helps that you included the exact error, steps, and what you observed right away.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis is a known issue we’re already tracking. It shows up exactly the way you described: memory writes via \u003ccode\u003eupdate_state\u003c/code\u003e (target: memory) fail with \u003ccode\u003ebrain docs snapshot was cut short before completing\u003c/code\u003e, while \u003ccode\u003eupdate_state\u003c/code\u003e with target: settings and direct file edits work fine. The fact that it happens on both new and old bots is expected for this issue, so it’s not caused by a single overloaded chat or anything in your setup.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eYour workaround is spot on. Have the bot write important facts directly into \u003ccode\u003ememory/profile.md\u003c/code\u003e or \u003ccode\u003ememory/log/YYYY-MM.md\u003c/code\u003e until this is fixed. You don’t need to run Update / Reset Computer for this, it won’t change anything.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eI can’t share a timeline yet, but I’ll post in this thread as soon as there’s an update.\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":5,"post_type":1,"posts_count":4,"updated_at":"2026-09-16T16:04:25.114Z","reply_count":1,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":1,"reads":4,"readers_count":3,"score":10.8,"yours":false,"topic_id":171895,"topic_slug":"grok-bot-update-state-memory-writes-fail-fleet-wide-brain-docs-snapshot-was-cut-short-before-completing","display_username":"Dean Rie","primary_group_name":"CursorStaff","flair_name":"CursorStaff","flair_url":"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/cursor1/original/3X/a/d/ad08adc640929ae1e98be69dab1ad0844cee99a0.png","flair_bg_color":"","flair_color":"","flair_group_id":42,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"read":true,"user_title":"","bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[],"moderator":true,"admin":true,"staff":true,"user_id":750,"hidden":false,"trust_level":4,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":false,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/grok-bot-update-state-memory-writes-fail-fleet-wide-brain-docs-snapshot-was-cut-short-before-completing/171895/5","reactions":[],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":0,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null},{"id":494256,"name":"","username":"doughy","avatar_template":"https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/d/c77e96/{size}.png","created_at":"2026-09-17T17:21:14.556Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eFollow-up (2026-09-17 ~10:10 AM America/Los_Angeles): \u003ccode\u003eupdate_state\u003c/code\u003e routine create/update also failing\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eSame Grok Bot / \u003ccode\u003eupdate_state\u003c/code\u003e surface as the memory/\u003ccode\u003ebrain docs\u003c/code\u003e issue in this thread, but a \u003cstrong\u003edifferent error string\u003c/strong\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-494256-agent-ids-reproduced-on-both-1\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-494256-agent-ids-reproduced-on-both-1\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eAgent IDs (reproduced on both)\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eChief of Staff: \u003ccode\u003ef283b3c0-75c5-41ac-a60b-455ef252740e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eDaily News: \u003ccode\u003eb703fc44-a58f-40fd-8fd6-5ecd482e9fd9\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-494256-whats-failing-now-2\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-494256-whats-failing-now-2\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eWhat’s failing now\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e\u003ccode\u003eupdate_state\u003c/code\u003e · target \u003ccode\u003eroutine\u003c/code\u003e · action \u003ccode\u003ecreate\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/strong\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\nError: \u003ccode\u003eNot saved — the routine could not be saved on the server this turn (create failed); try again in a moment.\u003c/code\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\nAttempted new routine name: \u003cstrong\u003eNews Briefing ship check\u003c/strong\u003e (schedule \u003ccode\u003e15 9 * * *\u003c/code\u003e). Disk staging only under \u003ccode\u003e…/automations/news-briefing-ship-check/\u003c/code\u003e — \u003cstrong\u003enot live on server\u003c/strong\u003e (\u003ccode\u003eupdate\u003c/code\u003e with that folder id → \u003ccode\u003eno routine with folder \"news-briefing-ship-check\" exists\u003c/code\u003e).\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e\u003ccode\u003eupdate_state\u003c/code\u003e · target \u003ccode\u003eroutine\u003c/code\u003e · action \u003ccode\u003eupdate\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/strong\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\nSame save error with \u003ccode\u003e(update failed)\u003c/code\u003e.\u003cbr\u003e\nTargeted existing routine: \u003cstrong\u003eYesterday fleet brief\u003c/strong\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eServer folder id: \u003ccode\u003ef46067a6-2734-57e3-a425-47b904b4f11e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eDisk path folder: \u003ccode\u003eyesterday-fleet-brief\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eAttempt: no-op schedule keep \u003ccode\u003e40 8 * * *\u003c/code\u003e (still failed)\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eDaily News also failed \u003cstrong\u003e3×\u003c/strong\u003e the same morning syncing routine folder \u003ccode\u003edaily-ai-tech-vc-briefing\u003c/code\u003e (display name \u003cstrong\u003eNews Briefing\u003c/strong\u003e, schedule \u003ccode\u003e30 8 * * *\u003c/code\u003e).\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-494256-still-failing-original-memory-bug-3\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-494256-still-failing-original-memory-bug-3\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eStill failing (original memory bug)\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e\u003ccode\u003eupdate_state\u003c/code\u003e · target \u003ccode\u003ememory\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/strong\u003e on CoS (\u003ccode\u003ef283b3c0-…\u003c/code\u003e)\u003cbr\u003e\nError: \u003ccode\u003eError: brain docs snapshot was cut short before completing\u003c/code\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\nRelated standing check: folder id \u003ccode\u003ememory-write-recovery-check\u003c/code\u003e (last run 2026-09-16 10:53:25 AM PT — failed).\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-494256-recent-success-for-bisect-4\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-494256-recent-success-for-bisect-4\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eRecent success (for bisect)\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e2026-09-16:\u003c/strong\u003e CoS successfully \u003cstrong\u003ecreated\u003c/strong\u003e Magok NR compare starts — folder id \u003ccode\u003emagok-nr-compare-starts\u003c/code\u003e, cron \u003ccode\u003e50 8 25 12 *\u003c/code\u003e.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e2026-09-16:\u003c/strong\u003e CoS successfully \u003cstrong\u003eupdated\u003c/strong\u003e Yesterday fleet brief (\u003ccode\u003ef46067a6-2734-57e3-a425-47b904b4f11e\u003c/code\u003e).\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eBy \u003cstrong\u003e2026-09-17 ~10:10 AM PT\u003c/strong\u003e, create \u003cstrong\u003eand\u003c/strong\u003e update both fail with the generic server-save message (not the brain-docs string).\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-494256-other-live-cos-routine-folder-ids-context-5\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-494256-other-live-cos-routine-folder-ids-context-5\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eOther live CoS routine folder ids (context)\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eWorkspace hygiene: \u003ccode\u003ec3c06169-af07-5f7c-a961-b03a458c554f\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eYesterday fleet brief: \u003ccode\u003ef46067a6-2734-57e3-a425-47b904b4f11e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eMemory write recovery check: \u003ccode\u003ememory-write-recovery-check\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eMagok NR compare starts: \u003ccode\u003emagok-nr-compare-starts\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-494256-impact-6\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-494256-impact-6\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eImpact\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eDisk edits to \u003ccode\u003eautomations/*/automation.json\u003c/code\u003e still work as workaround, but \u003cstrong\u003elive harness may not pick them up\u003c/strong\u003e until server sync succeeds. Blocks new standing routines and prompt updates via \u003ccode\u003eupdate_state\u003c/code\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-494256-ask-7\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-494256-ask-7\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eAsk\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003ePlease treat routine create/update save failures as in-scope with the memory/\u003ccode\u003ebrain docs\u003c/code\u003e incident (or confirm if separate). Happy to pull request/turn ids from client logs if you say which field you need.\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":7,"post_type":1,"posts_count":4,"updated_at":"2026-09-17T17:33:30.699Z","reply_count":1,"reply_to_post_number":5,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":0,"reads":3,"readers_count":2,"score":5.6,"yours":false,"topic_id":171895,"topic_slug":"grok-bot-update-state-memory-writes-fail-fleet-wide-brain-docs-snapshot-was-cut-short-before